Falsifies `system_tests::user::compositor_tests::a_client_cannot_read_any_page_of_its_neighbours_it_can_name`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: the spawner maps the neighbour's first pixel frame **read-only** into the client, at
the exact address the attacker is handed. Nothing writable moved, so the client still cannot
deface its neighbour, and everything it can see of the neighbour leaks.

Expected to fail: `assert!(wait_for(|| USER_FAULTS ... > faults), "a client READ its neighbour's
first pixel page at ... and was NOT stopped")`. Measured 2026-10-03 (UTC): red at the first pixel
page, after the control-page probe has passed.

**Measured on the same patch: the original test,
`a_client_holds_no_capability_for_its_neighbours_pixels_or_the_screen`, stays green.** Its probe is a
write, a write to a read-only page faults at the same address a write to an unmapped one does, and
the digests behind it only change if a write lands. That is the hole this test closes: the claim's
confidentiality half had no probe that could see a read-only exposure.

